 "section_summary": "This section contains the concluding pages of the American Embassy in Tokyo's monthly report on political and economic conditions in Japan for November 1939, followed by embassy schedules of despatches and telegrams sent to the Department of State during that month. The monthly report reviews domestic cabinet friction, the postponement of the proposed Trade Ministry, civil service reform debates, and financial difficulties including rising commodity inflation, rice shortages, and currency expansion under wartime controls. The accompanying registers enumerate seventy-five despatches and seventy-eight telegrams, documenting bilateral Japanese-American diplomatic discussions, Japanese-Soviet negotiations, and extensive reports of property losses and interference suffered by American missions and commercial firms across China.",
 "subfiles": [
